- Doctor, we shouldn't even be in here!

00:09:50.719 --> 00:09:51.966
Let us go!

00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:52.799
- We're thirsty too.

00:09:52.799 --> 00:09:54.360
We want orange juice now!

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.190
- My apologies, but a hospital can't allow

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:58.714
their violent patients
to run about freely.

00:09:58.714 --> 00:10:01.094
- And what does that mean?

00:10:01.094 --> 00:10:02.730
- A better life through lobotomies.

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:03.870
- Oh no.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.210
You know, Russia was one
of the first countries

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.640
to make lobotomies illegal,

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:11.010
and then the US ended up following suit

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.570
when it comes to psycho surgery.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.390
But psycho surgery is
still used to this day

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.240
in some very specific,
evidence based cases,

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:23.190
most notably making a
severance for epilepsy

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:25.770
that's drug resistant
in the corpus callosum,

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.530
which is the connection between
the two sides of the brain.

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:30.180
Actually, the person
who created lobotomies

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:31.830
won the Nobel Prize for it,

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.200
and then a lot of people have requested

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.600
that the Nobel Organization retrieve it

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.280
because they think it's too controversial.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.990
Tens of thousands of these were performed

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.853
with (peewoop) evidence.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.390
- Ew, look at Steve Smith.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.160
- Is it supposed to be curved like that?

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.567
- It can be.

00:10:48.567 --> 00:10:50.403
- Get that thing straightened out.

00:10:51.533 --> 00:10:53.580
(boys screaming)

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.870
- What are they talking about?

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:56.400
It's not curved, is it, fellas?

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.290
- All right, first, I'm not looking down.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.380
And second, they're
talking about your spine.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.030
You've got scoliosis.

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:04.770
- Were they talking about his spine?

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:07.590
And you can't really tell
scoliosis from that far away,

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:09.840
so I don't buy that. I mean,
you can if you can tell

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:11.190
that one shoulder's higher than the other,

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.380
one of the hips is higher than the other,

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.480
or maybe if even one of the rib angles

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.350
is higher than one of the other.

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:17.880
But then, you can usually see that

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.140
only when a person bends over.

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:21.480
- Pretty as a picture, scoliosis.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.010
- What do we do, amputate?

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.870
- Actually, all he
needs is a back support.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.780
- It really depends on something
known as the Cobb angle,

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:30.240
which is, after we order
a certain type of X-rays,

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.950
we can calculate this Cobb angle

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:34.110
and we see how bad the scoliosis is,

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:36.060
and most of them really are just treated

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:38.070
with conservative management,
like physical therapy.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:40.140
In some cases, we do bracing.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:43.050
In really advanced cases,
maybe surgery is an option,

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.880
but that's only when the curve is so bad

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.190
that it's compromising
your ability to breathe

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:48.720
or your heart to beat properly.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:49.920
- Is it like one of those belts

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.510
weightlifters wear at the Olympics

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:53.310
so they don't blow out their rectums?

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:56.400
- What, that's not why
weightlifters wear those.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.530
That looks terrible and
that's not what they wear.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:01.336
- I call her the chick
magnet, ironically, of course.

00:12:01.336 --> 00:12:03.600
No girl wants any of that.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.342
- I'll tell you why that device sucks,

00:12:05.342 --> 00:12:07.470
because you cannot take a deep breath.

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.790
So what it essentially is gonna do

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.590
is gonna cause you to
splint your breathing,

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:12.480
which means you're not
gonna take a deep breath,

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.730
which means that the
lower parts of your lungs,

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:17.730
the bases that really take
a lot of effort to fill,

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.700
won't fill, and therefore, you will have,

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:23.130
essentially, a loss of the
lower part of your lung,

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.960
known as atelectasis.

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.690
- Dad, I know it's only what's
on the inside that matters,

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:30.090
but I'm just not as
strong as (Steve gasps).

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:30.923
- Ooh!

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:33.660
- You're bald?

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:36.600
- Um, um, there's a kid on
the football team with cancer,

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:39.399
so the whole defensive line
shaved our heads in solidarity.

00:12:39.399 --> 00:12:40.232
- What?

00:12:40.232 --> 00:12:41.898
- Yeah, that was just nonsense. I'm bald.

00:12:41.898 --> 00:12:44.070
- I actually shaved my
head to stand in solidarity

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.180
with kids with cancer.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.040
Here's a picture, sorry
you had to see this.

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.409
- Guys, we have huge news.

00:12:49.409 --> 00:12:51.450
We're gonna start trying for a baby.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:52.283
- Ah!

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:55.920
- Steve, you're gonna be an uncle.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:56.753
- Ah!

00:12:56.753 --> 00:12:57.586
- I love the goldfish.

00:12:57.586 --> 00:12:59.160
- And what will I be?

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:02.913
- Oh, Claus, you'll be nearby.

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:06.450
And dad, you're gonna be a grandpa.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:10.023
- Why not make the goldfish the god fish?

00:13:10.966 --> 00:13:12.049
- [Sam] What?

00:13:12.954 --> 00:13:15.030
(Sam laughs)

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:16.560
Just keep smiling, baby.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.393
- You don't get it?

00:13:17.393 --> 00:13:18.226
- Just keep smiling.

00:13:18.226 --> 00:13:20.040
Why would, no I don't.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.060
- Everyone wants to be...

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:22.947
- [Sam] Like the godfather?
- Yeah, but the god fish.

00:13:22.947 --> 00:13:24.000
- [Sam] That's a bridge too far.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:24.833
- Come on!

00:13:24.833 --> 00:13:26.159
God fish, God father.

00:13:26.159 --> 00:13:27.420
(Sam groans)

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.130
And it's a goldfish!

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:29.963
There's a lot of...

00:13:29.963 --> 00:13:32.040
(Sam groans)

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.240
- [Sam] Objection.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.784
- I'm cooking breakfast
for my sweet daughter.

00:13:35.784 --> 00:13:36.930
- Aww, thanks Dad.

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:37.890
- Oh my God, please don't tell me

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:40.140
he's gonna put some kind of
medication in there for her

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:41.010
to end the pregnancy.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:41.913
No, he's not.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:44.580
No!

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.037
- Fresh squeezed OJ?

00:13:46.037 --> 00:13:47.640
- Jesus, that's evil.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.530
- Jeff, I wanted to take you out to dinner

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.440
to celebrate your efforts
to impregnate my daughter.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:54.140
And here we are at the restaurant.

00:13:55.124 --> 00:13:57.090
- Vasectomies.

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:58.620
- This place looks fancy.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:00.990
- A vasectomy is basically a permanent,

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:05.220
usually near 100% effective
form of birth control for men,

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:06.360
and it's called a vasectomy

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.900
because it blocks or
cuts your vas deferens,

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:13.350
which is the tube that carries
sperm from your testicle

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:16.980
to your peen.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:18.810
- How big is your minestrone?

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:21.660
- Is this man not aware he's
here for a medical procedure?

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:25.200
- Can you tell me a little bit
more about your colonoscopy?

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:26.400
Is that spicy?

00:14:29.203 --> 00:14:31.540
- I don't think this is
the best place to eat

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:33.340
for someone with your cholesterol.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:34.270
- Absolutely not.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.980
If you have high cholesterol
and you're eating foods

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.750
with high saturated fat content,

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:38.830
you're gonna run into troubles

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:40.090
'cause your cholesterol
will go even higher,

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:45.090
raising your 10 year risk
score of having ASCVD.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:47.230
- Stan, the doctor gave
you this health journal

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.480
to monitor your fitness and eating habits.

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:50.980
- Hey, if it ain't broke, don't fix it.

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:51.813
- It's broke.

00:14:51.813 --> 00:14:56.012
- And you heard my stool sample
results, too hard to test.

00:14:56.012 --> 00:14:57.670
- That's not a thing.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:59.230
- But you're getting older,

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.090
you need to take care of yourself.

00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:03.400
- Even when you're younger, you
should take care of yourself

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.770
'cause it'll pay dividends
for when you get older.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.420
- If he doesn't change his lifestyle,

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.980
something terrible could happen.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.410
- Sadly, people are
often set in their ways

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.120
until something really rattles them,

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:15.310
like a near death experience.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.480
- That's actually true,

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:18.760
or a loved one who really cares for them

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.611
encourages them to seek care.

00:15:20.611 --> 00:15:22.240
- What's with all the coffee?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.760
- After the amount of cheese
I consumed at Fuddrucker's,

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:25.930
it takes three pots worth

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:27.520
just to get my system running again.

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:28.780
- That's too much caffeine there.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.180
The maximum caffeine we
say safe to have in a day

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:33.550
is 400 milligrams, and I will say,

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.830
there are certain drinks at Starbucks,

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:39.550
a Venti Blonde Roast has 460 milligrams.

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:41.740
And then people put
espresso shots into those,

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:42.820
so be careful.

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:45.310
You're gonna start developing
some heart arrhythmias

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:47.710
if you keep pumping
that caffeine like that.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.610
These diseases,

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:51.310
I've literally only seen
in medical textbooks.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:53.980
Check out this video, lots
of great medical commentary.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:56.542
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:15:56.542 --> 00:15:59.125
(upbeat music)

